known_false_positives.description:
The newly added `None` is passed into `communicate_with_quorum`’s `grace_period` parameter (fraction of time-to-quorum, defaulting to `DEFAULT_GRACE_PERIOD`). This changes semantics vs. previous versions that had no explicit parameter. Please confirm the default grace period is desirable for these client operations (broadcasting chain info / sending chain update / receiving certs). If some of these paths are latency-sensitive, consider passing `Some(0.0)` to stop as soon as quorum is reached; if they benefit from collecting more responses (e.g., better error sampling / more votes), consider an explicit non-default value for clarity.

```suggestion
        communicate_with_quorum(
            &nodes,
            committee,
            |_: &()| (),
            |remote_node| {
                let mut updater = ValidatorUpdater {
                    chain_worker_count,
                    remote_node,
                    local_node: local_node.clone(),
                };
                Box::pin(async move {
                    updater
                        .send_chain_information(chain_id, height, delivery)
                        .await
                })
            },
            Some(0.0),
        )
```
